  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a number NNN, and your task is to determine whether it is a \"Good Number\" or not. A Good Number is defined as a number that is divisible by the sum of its own digits. If the number is divisible by the sum of its digits, it is classified as Good, otherwise, it is classified as Bad.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case contains a single integer NNN, the number you need to check.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print \"Good Number\" if the number is a Good, otherwise print \"Bad Number\".",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1061 \\leq N \\leq 10^61≤N≤106"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n18\n19\n21",
        "output": "Good Number\nBad Number\nGood Number",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: For the first test case, the sum of digits of 18 is 1+8=9. Since 18÷9=2, 18 is a Good Number.\nTest Case 2: For the second test case, the sum of digits of 19 is 1+9=10. Since 19÷10 is not an integer, 19 is a Bad Number.\nTest Case 3: For the third test case, the sum of digits of 21 is 2+1=3. Since 21÷3=7, 21 is a Good Number."
      }
    ]
  },
